WEBVTT

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:07.540
It is now 23:40 Greenwich Mean Time.

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:12.440
One world is about to end, and a new one is about to be born.

00:00:12.670 --> 00:00:15.720
The Earth Federation government is about to host a ceremony

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:17.640
at the Prime Minister's residence, "Laplace",

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:20.260
to usher in the birth of the new calendar era.

00:00:20.260 --> 00:00:23.060
Mankind has set foot into a new era,

00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:27.250
in which we shall build for ourselves worlds to live in, beyond Mother Earth.

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:32.380
Tonight, we shall become witnesses to history.

00:00:32.380 --> 00:00:35.310
Let us come together in this joyous moment

00:00:35.310 --> 00:00:40.740
and give thanks to the past, the Anno Domini era.

00:00:41.410 --> 00:00:47.170
Also, let us welcome in the dawn of the Universal Century with smiling faces.

00:00:47.810 --> 00:00:52.300
Goodbye, Anno Domini. Welcome, Universal Century!

00:00:54.170 --> 00:00:58.320
Greetings, citizens of Earth and space.

00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:04.430
I am the Prime Minister of the Earth Federation, Ricardo Marcenas.

00:01:04.430 --> 00:01:07.330
In a few moments, the Anno Domini era will come to an end.

00:01:07.330 --> 00:01:13.110
...Presidents and Prime Ministers spoke only to the citizens of their respective countries.

00:01:13.110 --> 00:01:17.110
These countries were composed of citizenries and territories,

00:01:17.110 --> 00:01:22.660
designed in the solitary interest of protecting their own security.

00:01:23.020 --> 00:01:28.460
Yet, as we've now realized humanity's long-awaited dream of a unified world government,

00:01:28.460 --> 00:01:30.520
we can look back on the antiquated nation-state system

00:01:30.520 --> 00:01:33.030
and see the problems that came with it.

00:01:33.470 --> 00:01:36.840
Just as no man is an island unto himself,

00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:41.600
a nation is incapable of functioning in a solitary vacuum.

00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:44.450
In regards to the threats to the planet as a whole,

00:01:44.450 --> 00:01:49.330
the nations of old were incapable of offering effective solutions.

00:01:49.330 --> 00:01:55.170
Rhetoric and sitting idly by are no longer options. We must...

00:02:58.030 --> 00:02:58.990
How is it?

00:03:01.380 --> 00:03:03.450
We'll go ahead as planned.

00:03:04.220 --> 00:03:07.950
This might cause more chaos than we've ever known.

00:03:09.540 --> 00:03:12.790
It's almost been one hundred years since then.

00:03:13.190 --> 00:03:17.800
As it stands, the Earth Sphere is approaching a dead end.

00:03:17.800 --> 00:03:25.240
Those who will correct the flaws of the Universal Century are beginning to emerge.

00:03:25.240 --> 00:03:31.710
I pray the one who can be entrusted to carry Laplace's Box is among them.

00:03:32.250 --> 00:03:33.330
Yes, sir.

00:03:34.810 --> 00:03:36.650
Cardeas...

00:03:39.070 --> 00:03:41.740
Do you... forgive me?

00:03:45.870 --> 00:03:49.830
This may lead to the end of a world.

00:03:49.830 --> 00:03:53.710
Who could forgive you besides me?

00:04:17.980 --> 00:04:21.730
Disperse Minovsky Particles at combat density, now!

00:04:21.730 --> 00:04:25.200
Enemy ship, appears to be Clop class... Thermal energy detected!

00:04:25.450 --> 00:04:26.700
Evasive maneuvers!

00:04:42.340 --> 00:04:44.340
What's taking so long with the bulkheads?!

00:04:44.840 --> 00:04:47.470
Intense heat sources emitted from enemy ship.

00:04:47.470 --> 00:04:49.930
Appears to be two mobile suits...

00:04:49.930 --> 00:04:51.930
No, three! Approaching at high speed!

00:04:52.430 --> 00:04:53.640
Send Marida out.

00:04:53.640 --> 00:04:57.400
Ignore the mothership. The Garencieres can shake it off.

00:04:57.400 --> 00:04:58.310
Roger that.

00:05:04.990 --> 00:05:06.030
Target acquired.

00:05:06.320 --> 00:05:09.530
There's a high-speed Jegan. Possibly a special forces version.

00:05:09.820 --> 00:05:14.540
That means this isn't a chance encounter. Ten minutes to the debris cluster.

00:05:14.540 --> 00:05:16.540
Wrap things up and get back here.

00:05:17.040 --> 00:05:18.540
Roger that, Master.

00:05:19.210 --> 00:05:20.840
Stop calling me that.

00:05:24.510 --> 00:05:27.010
Marida Cruz. Launching in Kshatriya!

00:05:45.780 --> 00:05:47.320
I won't let you follow our ship.

00:05:48.450 --> 00:05:49.450
Funnels!

00:07:23.000 --> 00:07:24.620
Damn Sleeves!

00:07:28.710 --> 00:07:31.800
Mission complete. Returning to ship.

00:07:47.150 --> 00:07:50.690
Thus, it was the Battle of A Baoa Qu

00:07:50.690 --> 00:07:53.200
which brought an end to the One Year War,

00:07:53.200 --> 00:07:57.740
started by the Principality of Zeon in the name of independence for the space emigrants.

00:07:57.740 --> 00:08:02.040
At the end of the war, over half of humanity was dead.

00:08:02.540 --> 00:08:08.290
This happened seventeen years ago, the year before you all were born.

00:08:08.540 --> 00:08:14.550
Even after the war, groups claiming to be the remnants of Zeon started wars of their own.

00:08:14.550 --> 00:08:19.260
They claim to desire autonomy for the Spacenoids, but at their heart

00:08:19.260 --> 00:08:22.770
you will still find the same ideas of the inherent superiority of the chosen elite

00:08:22.770 --> 00:08:25.230
found in the philosophy of Gihren Zabi.

00:08:25.230 --> 00:08:29.060
The concept of Zeonism proposed by Zeon Deikun, the so-called

00:08:29.070 --> 00:08:33.900
"Newtype" ideology, was a dangerous belief that ultimately

00:08:33.900 --> 00:08:36.820
produced rebellious elements such as these.

00:08:38.370 --> 00:08:39.530
You there!

00:08:39.990 --> 00:08:44.750
Don't blow off studying history because you think it won't help get you a job!

00:08:45.080 --> 00:08:49.290
Anaheim won't even hire you for a factory worker position,

00:08:49.290 --> 00:08:51.250
if you're not capable of passing senior high.

00:08:51.250 --> 00:08:55.340
Don't believe everything you hear about that 100% job placement rate–

00:08:55.340 --> 00:08:57.720
Mr. Bancroft, it's the shuttle again...

00:09:04.770 --> 00:09:07.810
It's seriously time to upgrade our shuttles.

00:09:07.810 --> 00:09:09.600
The chairman's just a cheapskate.

00:09:09.600 --> 00:09:12.110
He thinks that the decommissioned Anaheim ones are fine.

00:09:12.110 --> 00:09:14.650
So we're staying here tonight?

00:09:14.650 --> 00:09:15.940
I didn't bring a change of clothes.

00:09:15.950 --> 00:09:16.700
Neither did I.

00:09:17.280 --> 00:09:20.780
Which means we won't get to go on the field trip to see the Snail tomorrow.

00:09:20.780 --> 00:09:26.290
What?! I don't want to spend two days here listening to Bancroft's "special" lectures!

00:09:26.290 --> 00:09:30.080
I could teach all the way to Char's Rebellion in two minutes.

00:09:30.380 --> 00:09:32.090
Right, Banagher?

00:09:34.710 --> 00:09:38.220
Wow, look at that! It's a Zaku!

00:09:39.340 --> 00:09:40.800
Damn it, Bancroft.

00:09:40.800 --> 00:09:43.890
Why didn't you tell us there was something this cool here?

00:09:43.890 --> 00:09:45.850
What's that? Is it something cool?

00:09:46.770 --> 00:09:49.020
It's the granddaddy of all mobile suits!

00:09:49.020 --> 00:09:49.810
Oh...?

00:09:49.810 --> 00:09:51.860
Hey, wait up. Let's check it out.

00:09:52.230 --> 00:09:53.400
Don't care.

00:09:53.400 --> 00:09:56.650
The wars ended a long time ago. We don't need those things anymore.

00:09:56.650 --> 00:09:58.860
I'm pretty sure you aren't allowed to take pictures.

00:09:58.860 --> 00:10:02.120
You guys have no sense of adventure, seriously.

00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:12.880
Say, Banagher,

00:10:13.290 --> 00:10:16.130
you know sometimes you look like you're staring out into the distance.

00:10:16.130 --> 00:10:16.840
Yeah?

00:10:16.840 --> 00:10:18.340
Yeah. You just did it back there.

00:10:19.090 --> 00:10:21.800
I'm not really looking at anything in particular when I do that...

00:10:22.180 --> 00:10:22.800
Huh?

00:10:23.970 --> 00:10:27.060
I think I'm just wondering where...

00:10:27.890 --> 00:10:29.350
Where your father is?

00:10:29.350 --> 00:10:31.020
No, where I am.

00:10:31.020 --> 00:10:32.060
Oh, sorry.

00:10:32.690 --> 00:10:36.820
Like whatever I'm doing... I'm not really there, you know?

00:10:36.820 --> 00:10:42.280
I have the same feeling. Like something's just off, right?

00:10:42.280 --> 00:10:43.280
Yeah...

00:10:45.200 --> 00:10:48.830
I wonder if it's gonna keep getting stronger and stronger.

00:10:49.710 --> 00:10:55.670
I think the only ones who don't feel it are the few who get to live their lives how they want to.

00:11:02.340 --> 00:11:04.430
Hey, are you listening to me?

00:11:09.680 --> 00:11:10.810
A mobile suit...

00:11:26.780 --> 00:11:28.240
Keep the speed going.

00:11:28.240 --> 00:11:29.240
Y-Yes, sir.

00:11:32.920 --> 00:11:35.960
Fly like you're going straight into that debris field.

00:11:42.840 --> 00:11:44.050
Keep going.

00:11:46.470 --> 00:11:47.800
Sir!

00:11:49.060 --> 00:11:50.680
Breakdown 0-6-0.

00:12:01.070 --> 00:12:02.780
Impressive.

00:12:02.780 --> 00:12:03.900
Th-Thank you.

00:12:03.900 --> 00:12:05.290
I'm talking about the machine.

00:12:05.290 --> 00:12:06.450
Yes, sir.

00:12:06.450 --> 00:12:07.780
Good job.

00:12:17.920 --> 00:12:19.550
We're going back, Gael.

00:12:20.090 --> 00:12:21.800
I'm sorry, sir.

00:12:21.800 --> 00:12:22.670
What's wrong?

00:12:22.970 --> 00:12:27.140
It appears there were still people at the Anaheim Electronics Industrial College training facility.

00:12:27.140 --> 00:12:29.510
I thought we checked the class schedule...

00:12:29.810 --> 00:12:32.470
It seems the transit shuttle broke down.

00:12:32.480 --> 00:12:36.940
I see... Well, even if someone noticed it,

00:12:36.940 --> 00:12:40.020
it couldn't have been more than a momentary glimpse.

00:12:45.450 --> 00:12:48.490
I was able to get hold of a staff officer on Luna II.

00:12:48.990 --> 00:12:54.000
It's true, a Londo Bell ship ran into some Sleeves.

00:12:54.000 --> 00:12:57.000
So there was a leak... Was there a battle?

00:12:57.000 --> 00:13:00.840
Yes. Not only did they lose three mobile suits, but they let them get away.

00:13:00.840 --> 00:13:02.000
Anything else?

00:13:02.000 --> 00:13:05.510
I tried Londenion, but their commander is a very tight-lipped person.

00:13:05.800 --> 00:13:07.930
Bright Noa, is it?

00:13:07.930 --> 00:13:11.010
Try the supply fleets, then. You'll be able to figure out how the fleet itself is moving.

00:13:11.010 --> 00:13:11.470
Certainly.

00:13:12.350 --> 00:13:14.430
Everyone, listen up.

00:13:14.430 --> 00:13:18.850
All operational testing of the RX-0 is now finished.

00:13:18.850 --> 00:13:21.940
We are to immediately delete the testing OS.

00:13:21.940 --> 00:13:25.950
Seal the NT-D, and boot up the Laplace Program.

00:13:52.890 --> 00:13:54.350
"Forgive", huh?

00:14:16.200 --> 00:14:18.620
Roger that. Entering gate #5.

00:14:18.620 --> 00:14:21.620
What is this "Laplace's Box" thing?

00:14:22.080 --> 00:14:26.380
If they really have it, we'll bring it back home. If it's a trap, we'll fight our way out.

00:15:53.380 --> 00:15:59.060
Man, this weightlessness is getting to me. Lemme skip the Snail field trip.

00:15:59.060 --> 00:16:01.560
It's 'cause you were partying all night.

00:16:01.560 --> 00:16:04.060
I just don't find looking at the Construction Unit all that interesting.

00:16:04.060 --> 00:16:07.020
But guys, it's not often people get to see the inside of that thing.

00:16:12.070 --> 00:16:13.030
Banagher!

00:16:13.030 --> 00:16:14.060
Don't ask, Micott.

00:16:13.700 --> 00:16:15.070
Banagher, bathroom?

00:16:15.070 --> 00:16:16.820
I'm going back ahead of you guys!

00:16:16.240 --> 00:16:17.990
That looks bad over there.

00:16:24.210 --> 00:16:25.540
I can't die...

00:16:34.510 --> 00:16:35.930
Hey! What're you doing?!

00:16:36.220 --> 00:16:37.350
I'm borrowing this.

00:16:37.350 --> 00:16:39.970
Like hell you are! Hey, wait! Hey!

00:16:43.140 --> 00:16:45.060
Ah! Hey!

00:16:46.020 --> 00:16:47.520
It's not like being in a vacuum.

00:16:53.400 --> 00:16:56.530
Found you, but it's almost daybreak... This is bad.

00:16:59.490 --> 00:17:01.620
I'm not yet...

00:17:22.470 --> 00:17:23.680
Danger. Danger.

00:17:30.150 --> 00:17:31.190
I'll get us through this.

00:17:44.410 --> 00:17:45.500
Clench your teeth!

00:17:50.000 --> 00:17:51.330
Danger. Danger.

00:18:00.750 --> 00:18:02.260
Banagher, wake up.

00:18:04.140 --> 00:18:05.680
Banagher, wake up.

00:18:24.160 --> 00:18:25.240
Ow-ow-ow...

00:18:25.240 --> 00:18:25.910
Who are you?!

00:18:25.910 --> 00:18:26.790
What do you think you're doing?!

00:18:26.910 --> 00:18:29.160
Banagher, are you OK? Banagher?

00:18:29.540 --> 00:18:30.790
Are you from this colony?

00:18:32.790 --> 00:18:36.750
I'm in a hurry. Can you give me a lift to the Colony Builder's entrance?

00:18:37.380 --> 00:18:38.840
To the Snail?

00:18:38.840 --> 00:18:40.550
Will this thing still work?

00:18:40.550 --> 00:18:42.930
It's out of gas. The battery's dead too.

00:18:42.930 --> 00:18:44.890
I'm running out of time! Please!

00:18:45.510 --> 00:18:48.120
There's someone I absolutely must speak with.

00:18:48.120 --> 00:18:50.890
If we don't hurry, something will happen that can never be undone.

00:18:50.890 --> 00:18:53.400
But we can still prevent it if we act fast. So please...

00:18:53.730 --> 00:18:55.730
Prevent it? Prevent what?

00:18:56.190 --> 00:18:56.980
War.

00:19:03.200 --> 00:19:04.320
Hold on!

00:19:09.830 --> 00:19:11.410
You can't do this alone.

00:19:15.480 --> 00:19:17.550
Who do you need to see?

00:19:19.880 --> 00:19:21.050
The Snail...

00:19:21.300 --> 00:19:26.010
That's what everyone calls the Colony Builder, but it's nothing more than a factory there.

00:19:26.350 --> 00:19:30.020
I heard a rumor that there's a Vist Foundation mansion at the end of it, though.

00:19:31.770 --> 00:19:32.730
You know them?

00:19:32.730 --> 00:19:39.070
No, I've never been there, but one of their higher-ups is the chairman of my school.

00:19:44.320 --> 00:19:46.990
This is an announcement for all passengers.

00:19:46.990 --> 00:19:50.580
The authorities have just issued a security alert.

00:19:50.910 --> 00:19:55.040
This train will be stopping temporarily at this station.

00:19:55.040 --> 00:19:59.960
We will resume once everyone's safety has been confirmed. Your patience is appreciated.

00:19:56.290 --> 00:19:57.920
Seriously? Again?

00:19:57.920 --> 00:19:59.960
Everyone's been nervous lately.

00:19:59.960 --> 00:20:01.630
Let's get off here.

00:20:01.630 --> 00:20:03.630
We can't, Marco!

00:20:07.010 --> 00:20:07.890
Let's get off.

00:20:12.390 --> 00:20:15.350
You think she was in that Petit MS?

00:20:15.350 --> 00:20:18.730
Probably. Given the fact she's disappeared.

00:20:18.730 --> 00:20:21.650
We're in real trouble if the Federation saw her.

00:20:21.650 --> 00:20:24.490
But we'll have to see how the Foundation acts to determine that.

00:20:24.950 --> 00:20:26.570
My apologies, sir.

00:20:26.570 --> 00:20:29.450
I should have noticed her stowing away...

00:20:29.450 --> 00:20:34.080
You have no reason to apologize. As captain of this ship, I take full responsibility.

00:20:34.710 --> 00:20:36.710
I can wager a guess as to where she's going.

00:20:36.710 --> 00:20:40.800
Go on ahead of her and bring her back before she makes contact with Cardeas Vist.

00:20:40.800 --> 00:20:42.090
And try to stay under the radar.

00:20:45.430 --> 00:20:48.050
That's a Construction Unit?

00:20:48.050 --> 00:20:51.970
Yeah, it's a factory unit that builds foundation blocks for the colony.

00:20:51.970 --> 00:20:55.310
This colony's still under construction.

00:20:56.690 --> 00:21:02.190
Eat up, you must be starving. This'll save time.

00:21:03.860 --> 00:21:06.360
You expect me to eat while walking...?

00:21:11.330 --> 00:21:13.490
They're about to begin a factory tour.

00:21:13.490 --> 00:21:16.500
Let's mingle in with them. We'll figure out the rest once we're in there.

00:21:37.440 --> 00:21:38.850
Marida...?

00:21:41.690 --> 00:21:45.440
Let's go back. You need to consider your position–

00:21:45.440 --> 00:21:48.530
It's because of my position that I've come here.

00:21:49.490 --> 00:21:51.490
Please stop this futility.

00:21:51.490 --> 00:21:55.370
We can't handle Laplace's Box right now.

00:21:55.370 --> 00:22:01.000
Whatever it is, it will simply be used by Full Frontal to start a useless war.

00:22:01.380 --> 00:22:02.790
You understand, right?

00:22:02.790 --> 00:22:06.260
I don't understand. I'm just following orders.

00:22:06.380 --> 00:22:10.260
Lies. You weren't given your power for this...

00:22:10.430 --> 00:22:11.390
I'm sorry.

00:22:15.970 --> 00:22:17.100
Danger! Danger!

00:22:19.600 --> 00:22:21.150
Give me your hand.

00:22:46.050 --> 00:22:46.750
Hurry!

00:22:46.750 --> 00:22:47.340
Huh?

00:23:31.510 --> 00:23:32.090
Why...?

00:23:32.090 --> 00:23:32.760
My name...

00:23:32.760 --> 00:23:33.430
Huh?

00:23:33.680 --> 00:23:36.430
I apologize. I never told you my name. It's...

00:23:36.430 --> 00:23:37.470
Banagher.

00:23:37.470 --> 00:23:37.890
Huh?

00:23:37.890 --> 00:23:39.470
It called out your name before.

00:23:39.470 --> 00:23:41.430
Go, Banagher. Banagher.

00:23:41.430 --> 00:23:43.480
That's right. Banagher Links.

00:23:43.480 --> 00:23:44.980
I'm...

00:23:45.810 --> 00:23:48.770
Audrey. Audrey Burne.

00:23:48.780 --> 00:23:50.030
Audrey?

00:23:50.030 --> 00:23:50.900
This here is Haro.

00:23:50.900 --> 00:23:52.150
Have you heard of it?

00:23:52.150 --> 00:23:56.490
It's a replica of a robot mascot built by an ace pilot back during the war.

00:23:56.490 --> 00:23:58.660
It was all the rage when we were kids.

00:23:58.660 --> 00:24:00.910
Well, I lived out in the boonies, so...

00:24:00.910 --> 00:24:02.040
The boonies...?

00:24:02.040 --> 00:24:07.170
Or rather... I guess I came into this life as a vagabond.

00:24:08.550 --> 00:24:10.500
Then, you're just like me.

00:24:14.840 --> 00:24:17.050
Wow! Would you look at those rails!

00:24:17.050 --> 00:24:18.850
No way! That's so high up!

00:24:18.850 --> 00:24:21.680
Man! That framework is something else.

00:24:22.520 --> 00:24:25.060
Come take a look at this, Micott. It's incredible.

00:24:26.770 --> 00:24:28.690
Banagher never made it, huh?

00:24:28.690 --> 00:24:32.280
Yeah... That Petit MS that supposedly crashed on our school campus...

00:24:32.280 --> 00:24:33.530
Maybe it was him, after all...

00:24:33.860 --> 00:24:36.200
It didn't crash, it was a forced landing.

00:24:36.200 --> 00:24:40.030
I don't know why he did it, but you shouldn't go spreading rumors.

00:24:40.040 --> 00:24:41.040
Huh?

00:24:41.040 --> 00:24:44.160
He's going to be out on the street if he gets kicked out of school.

00:24:44.160 --> 00:24:46.540
He's got no home to return to.

00:24:52.920 --> 00:24:54.010
Banagher?!

00:24:55.010 --> 00:24:57.010
Who's that girl?

00:24:57.300 --> 00:25:00.100
Those people after you... What's their story?

00:25:00.640 --> 00:25:02.060
They're my comrades.

00:25:02.060 --> 00:25:04.640
They're after me because I ran away.

00:25:04.890 --> 00:25:07.190
Are you a political activist or something?

00:25:09.230 --> 00:25:11.570
You know, those anti-Federation...

00:25:11.570 --> 00:25:14.360
The ones seeking independence for the Spacenoids or whatever.

00:25:14.360 --> 00:25:18.030
Yeah. Only scarier than them.

00:25:18.030 --> 00:25:20.870
You did say you wanted to prevent a war, right?

00:25:21.030 --> 00:25:22.240
You...

00:25:33.670 --> 00:25:38.340
The colony's walls are growing as more and more foundation blocks are added.

00:25:38.340 --> 00:25:42.760
It's incredible... The world is expanding.

00:26:02.160 --> 00:26:06.160
Sir, the surveillance camera on lift #2 just spotted something.

00:26:07.710 --> 00:26:08.910
What's she doing there?

00:26:08.920 --> 00:26:10.290
I don't know, sir.

00:26:10.290 --> 00:26:12.710
We were told that, early this morning, someone snuck into

00:26:12.710 --> 00:26:17.210
the service route to the artificial sun, but I never expected...

00:26:17.220 --> 00:26:19.130
Have you heard from the Sleeves?

00:26:19.130 --> 00:26:19.930
No.

00:26:23.260 --> 00:26:25.390
So she's acting on her own?

00:26:25.390 --> 00:26:28.600
Her presence may interfere with the Box's delivery.

00:26:28.600 --> 00:26:31.400
I still think that you, the head of the Vist Foundation,

00:26:31.400 --> 00:26:34.860
meeting with the Sleeves in person isn't...

00:26:35.730 --> 00:26:37.690
And... this boy here?

00:26:37.690 --> 00:26:40.070
Yes, sir. He was with her.

00:26:40.070 --> 00:26:42.740
He looks a bit young for a bodyguard...

00:26:53.130 --> 00:26:56.960
That's it. I can't believe there's really a mansion here.

00:27:07.680 --> 00:27:09.430
Maybe no one's here...

00:27:12.310 --> 00:27:13.400
Banagher?

00:27:13.940 --> 00:27:16.400
Excuse us, is anyone home?

00:27:23.370 --> 00:27:25.200
Banagher, you can't just–

00:27:33.710 --> 00:27:35.250
A unicorn...

00:27:38.340 --> 00:27:41.760
"To my only desire..."

00:27:41.760 --> 00:27:43.720
You can read that?

00:27:44.260 --> 00:27:49.430
What the heck? I know this. I've seen that image before.

00:27:49.430 --> 00:27:51.390
I see you're curious about that.

00:27:51.940 --> 00:27:53.980
"The Lady and the Unicorn".

00:27:53.980 --> 00:27:58.270
It's a tapestry believed to have been created in France before the middle era.

00:27:58.270 --> 00:28:00.400
And it's not a replica.

00:28:00.400 --> 00:28:04.240
My predecessor went through a great deal of trouble to obtain it, prior to the One Year War.

00:28:04.490 --> 00:28:07.740
I'm the head of the family, Cardeas Vist.

00:28:08.080 --> 00:28:12.250
I apologize for coming into your home without permission. I'm...

00:28:12.460 --> 00:28:14.460
I'm aware of who you are.

00:28:14.460 --> 00:28:17.750
Do yourself a favor and don't mention your name.

00:28:18.130 --> 00:28:19.880
I won't give my name, then.

00:28:19.880 --> 00:28:23.880
As long as you understand my position, that's sufficient.

00:28:24.430 --> 00:28:27.510
I've come here to ask you to rethink what you're doing.

00:28:27.510 --> 00:28:31.720
I'm referring to your plan to give Laplace's Box to us.

00:28:33.560 --> 00:28:35.690
You'd best go home.

00:28:36.270 --> 00:28:40.520
It's dangerous. I shouldn't be talking to you under these circumstances.

00:28:40.530 --> 00:28:44.700
Zinnerman is a rational man. He wouldn't cause any unnecessary trouble.

00:28:45.030 --> 00:28:48.780
Would protecting you be considered unnecessary?

00:28:48.780 --> 00:28:49.830
Why are you doing this?

00:28:49.830 --> 00:28:50.950
I've heard that Laplace's Box

00:28:50.950 --> 00:28:55.040
has guaranteed the prosperity of the Vist Foundation for decades.

00:28:55.040 --> 00:28:56.370
Why are you giving it to us?

00:28:56.370 --> 00:28:58.710
Excuse me. I believe I asked you to leave.

00:28:59.880 --> 00:29:02.720
There are people after her. I can't leave her alone.

00:29:02.880 --> 00:29:07.220
Do you know who they are, or why they're after her?

00:29:07.760 --> 00:29:10.550
I don't. But they're scary people.

00:29:10.890 --> 00:29:12.060
Scary?

00:29:12.060 --> 00:29:13.600
That's how they feel to me.

00:29:13.600 --> 00:29:16.020
That's something a Newtype would say.

00:29:16.480 --> 00:29:17.810
That's what she said.

00:29:18.230 --> 00:29:20.940
You're putting your future at risk by staying here.

00:29:20.940 --> 00:29:26.820
It's not what your father intended when he sent you to Anaheim Electronics Industrial College.

00:29:26.820 --> 00:29:27.780
How do you...?

00:29:28.160 --> 00:29:30.240
I'm the chairman, after all.

00:29:30.240 --> 00:29:36.080
As such, I can find out who my students are and I even have the authority to expel the bad apples.

00:29:37.540 --> 00:29:39.630
Go back, Banagher.

00:29:39.830 --> 00:29:42.250
Thank you for bringing me here.

00:29:42.250 --> 00:29:43.960
I can handle the rest.

00:29:44.340 --> 00:29:46.800
I can help you, Audrey.

00:29:46.800 --> 00:29:48.970
You came here to prevent a war, didn't you?

00:29:48.970 --> 00:29:51.470
Doesn't he have the power to do that?

00:29:51.850 --> 00:29:56.180
Hearing you talk about war just feels different from when my professors talk about it.

00:29:56.180 --> 00:30:00.480
It feels more grave... I understand how frightening it will be, so...

00:30:00.480 --> 00:30:01.860
So please...

00:30:01.860 --> 00:30:02.980
Banagher...

00:30:03.270 --> 00:30:07.570
My heart was pounding when I saw you fall from the sky this morning.

00:30:07.570 --> 00:30:09.990
Everything that felt off in my life just slid into place,

00:30:09.990 --> 00:30:13.410
and for the first time, I saw where I needed to be.

00:30:13.410 --> 00:30:17.540
I don't care who you are! Just tell me you need me!

00:30:17.540 --> 00:30:18.420
If you do that, I'll...

00:30:19.370 --> 00:30:20.420
I don't need you.

00:30:23.800 --> 00:30:26.880
The best thing you can do is forget you ever met me.

00:30:40.560 --> 00:30:42.900
It was the right decision.

00:30:42.900 --> 00:30:46.020
I've changed the designated location of my transaction with your comrades.

00:30:46.030 --> 00:30:48.900
I'll reunite you with them when the time seems right.

00:30:48.900 --> 00:30:51.150
I plead with you to change your mind...

00:30:51.160 --> 00:30:53.570
I understand your concern over the situation.

00:30:53.570 --> 00:31:00.410
I'm aware that they're calling Full Frontal the second coming of Char.

00:31:00.420 --> 00:31:01.160
So then...

00:31:01.830 --> 00:31:05.670
But, even if given the key,

00:31:05.670 --> 00:31:10.630
someone without the appropriate talents will be unable to open Laplace's Box.

00:31:11.890 --> 00:31:13.590
The key to the... Box?

00:31:13.590 --> 00:31:19.100
We've done something to it that ensures this. It's no easy horse to break.

00:31:21.060 --> 00:31:23.440
That's enough. Go back to the ship.

00:31:24.190 --> 00:31:26.440
We received a message from the Foundation.

00:31:26.440 --> 00:31:30.690
They want to move the transaction site from the Central Port to the Colony Builder.

00:31:31.030 --> 00:31:32.700
What about her?

00:31:32.990 --> 00:31:34.990
They're feigning ignorance.

00:31:34.990 --> 00:31:39.200
I can't tell what they're up to, but we'll have to keep a poker face for now.

00:31:39.950 --> 00:31:43.920
Go back to the ship. Be ready for anything.

00:31:51.170 --> 00:31:52.420
Huh? What's that?

00:32:05.730 --> 00:32:08.940
I'm honored that the head of the Vist family is meeting us himself.

00:32:09.360 --> 00:32:12.530
We're entrusting you with the fate of the Foundation.

00:32:12.530 --> 00:32:14.740
I couldn't let another man handle this task.

00:32:14.990 --> 00:32:16.160
Come this way.

00:32:18.990 --> 00:32:20.450
Piece of junk!

00:32:27.090 --> 00:32:28.040
Londo Bell?

00:32:28.630 --> 00:32:30.630
What're they doing here?!

00:32:34.380 --> 00:32:35.550
The enemy?

00:32:36.300 --> 00:32:38.550
It's... a key?

00:32:38.550 --> 00:32:42.060
So it's not the Box itself you're giving us, but rather... its key?

00:32:42.350 --> 00:32:43.810
Unsatisfied?

00:32:44.020 --> 00:32:46.440
Not unsatisfied, just confused.

00:32:46.440 --> 00:32:51.400
We don't even know what the Box is.

00:32:51.400 --> 00:32:55.820
We know that opening Laplace's Box would mean overthrowing the Federation.

00:32:55.820 --> 00:33:00.080
And that the Vist Foundation's wealth and glory come from your secret possession of it.

00:33:00.080 --> 00:33:06.120
Your status as a charity that transports works of art to the colonies is just a front.

00:33:06.120 --> 00:33:07.210
The truth is...

00:33:07.210 --> 00:33:10.590
Your leaders acknowledged the Box's value,

00:33:10.590 --> 00:33:14.050
which is why they sent a man of your skill here.

00:33:14.050 --> 00:33:20.550
In our current situation, we can't afford to not grab at any bait that's dangled in front of us.

00:33:20.560 --> 00:33:25.560
If it turns out to be poisoned, then I guess my superiors will be disappointed.

00:33:25.560 --> 00:33:29.560
Do you believe that Newtypes exist, Captain?

00:33:30.060 --> 00:33:35.440
Spend time on the battlefield, and you'll run into powers that you can only explain that way.

00:33:35.450 --> 00:33:39.950
"Power." That's a word someone who's physically felt it would use.

00:33:40.120 --> 00:33:42.030
As humanity expands into space,

00:33:42.040 --> 00:33:47.290
all our latent abilities will blossom in order to adapt to that great void,

00:33:47.290 --> 00:33:49.960
and we'll be able to understand each other without misconceptions.

00:33:50.540 --> 00:33:54.250
That's the Newtype theory once proposed by Zeon Deikun,

00:33:54.250 --> 00:34:01.090
which spoke of the reformation of humanity and infinite possibilities... of "power" itself.

00:34:04.430 --> 00:34:06.310
Damn it!

00:34:20.240 --> 00:34:22.120
Garencieres! Enemies are here!

00:34:22.120 --> 00:34:24.240
Londo Bell is about to surround the colony!

00:34:24.700 --> 00:34:27.250
Since its victory in the One Year War,

00:34:27.250 --> 00:34:31.980
the Federation has lived in fear of this unseen power.

00:34:31.980 --> 00:34:35.500
The power that shouts "J'accuse" at the privileged class that lives on Earth.

00:34:35.500 --> 00:34:39.260
The power that calls to the abandoned Spacenoids to awaken.

00:34:40.800 --> 00:34:41.760
What?!

00:34:49.480 --> 00:34:53.150
A power that may overthrow the control of the Federation government

00:34:53.150 --> 00:34:54.940
which has lasted nearly a hundred years.

00:34:55.110 --> 00:34:57.940
Space belongs to the Spacenoids!

00:35:10.500 --> 00:35:16.000
The Federation has been absorbed for decades now in a battle against this invisible "Power".

00:35:16.340 --> 00:35:22.760
D-Damn dogs whose souls are still chained to Earth!

00:35:27.720 --> 00:35:30.770
Long live Neo Zeon!

00:35:52.210 --> 00:35:53.500
What was that?! An explosion?!

00:35:53.880 --> 00:35:56.210
Gilboa, have you heard from the Captain?

00:35:56.210 --> 00:35:58.750
I lost the connection. The Minovsky Particles are getting denser!

00:35:59.210 --> 00:36:01.210
Attack them inside?

00:36:01.220 --> 00:36:03.760
The enemy has surrounded the colony. Our only option is to cut straight through.

00:36:03.760 --> 00:36:05.510
We'll find the Captain and get the hell out of here.

00:36:05.510 --> 00:36:06.760
Roger.

00:36:06.760 --> 00:36:10.770
It's true that government research facilities were created.

00:36:10.770 --> 00:36:15.650
But they were just mad scientists' labs, intended to artificially enhance

00:36:15.650 --> 00:36:19.570
the weapon-like aspects of Newtypes alone.

00:36:24.240 --> 00:36:30.990
The civil conflict known as the Gryps War and also the two Neo Zeon wars...

00:36:33.580 --> 00:36:37.380
In all these cases, harsh oppression led to the rise of military factions,

00:36:37.380 --> 00:36:40.340
and the Federation suffered great harm.

00:36:40.340 --> 00:36:45.970
However, it had a strong ally that ultimately secured its victory.

00:36:47.470 --> 00:36:49.060
Do you know to what I refer?

00:36:49.220 --> 00:36:50.850
Time?

00:36:50.850 --> 00:36:52.270
Indeed.

00:36:52.270 --> 00:36:55.310
The public sought results,

00:36:55.310 --> 00:37:00.530
and it grew tired of the "Newtypes" which held no strict definition, only possibility.

00:37:01.400 --> 00:37:05.450
The term "Newtype" eventually became synonymous with "ace pilot",

00:37:05.450 --> 00:37:08.240
a definition as far as possible from the original concept

00:37:08.240 --> 00:37:10.580
of understanding without misconceptions

00:37:10.580 --> 00:37:13.580
proposed by Zeon Deikun.

00:37:14.710 --> 00:37:16.330
Hey, look at that.

00:37:16.710 --> 00:37:18.460
Hey, what's that?

00:37:21.300 --> 00:37:24.800
Laplace's Box holds the power to change the future.

00:37:24.800 --> 00:37:27.630
Or rather, I suppose we should say

00:37:27.630 --> 00:37:29.930
the power to restore the future we were meant to have.

00:37:29.930 --> 00:37:32.810
However, not all men have the ability to wield it.

00:37:33.350 --> 00:37:37.810
If it's misused, it could destroy the world.

00:37:37.810 --> 00:37:41.440
So you're going to give us the key as a test, to start?

00:37:41.820 --> 00:37:46.530
If, hypothetically, you're small-minded enough that you focus only on a single thing,

00:37:46.530 --> 00:37:49.070
the Box will not reveal its contents.

00:37:49.320 --> 00:37:50.820
That single thing being?

00:37:51.660 --> 00:37:53.830
The revival of Zeon.

00:38:27.360 --> 00:38:32.780
It's Londo Bell. Combat has already begun inside the colony.

00:38:32.780 --> 00:38:34.490
Have you contacted the military?

00:38:34.490 --> 00:38:38.660
Are you saying we've been caught in a trap?

00:38:38.660 --> 00:38:43.670
I'd say you were followed here, but neither of us can prove it.

00:38:44.130 --> 00:38:46.130
We'll be taking her back.

00:38:46.130 --> 00:38:51.130
I was always planning on returning her to you. She's safe, in my mansion.

00:38:54.140 --> 00:38:59.600
It's very difficult for one person to trust another. It's unfortunate, sir.

00:39:00.440 --> 00:39:02.600
I feel the same way, Captain.

00:39:11.530 --> 00:39:12.700
Get everyone out of here!

00:39:29.420 --> 00:39:30.590
Get off my tail, damn it!

00:39:37.310 --> 00:39:38.270
So heavy!

00:39:52.610 --> 00:39:53.860
This'll shut you up!

00:40:10.420 --> 00:40:11.550
Hurry!

00:40:31.490 --> 00:40:33.110
There are holes in the colony.

00:40:33.110 --> 00:40:34.990
The school's around there.

00:40:34.990 --> 00:40:39.160
It's war. War has broken out.

00:40:39.830 --> 00:40:41.160
War...

00:40:51.510 --> 00:40:52.670
Audrey!

00:40:54.470 --> 00:40:55.840
Wait, Banagher!

00:40:55.840 --> 00:40:57.470
H-Hey!

00:41:17.950 --> 00:41:19.200
Sir.

00:41:19.200 --> 00:41:23.160
It's a shame that a hundred year old alliance can be broken so easily.

00:41:23.160 --> 00:41:26.120
The Federation is using this as an opportunity to take it all away.

00:41:26.540 --> 00:41:30.630
Of course, we were the ones who tried to scrap it first.

00:41:30.630 --> 00:41:33.760
Gael, don't let the Federation have it!

00:42:19.010 --> 00:42:20.680
We can't get out of here?!

00:42:23.560 --> 00:42:25.560
Hey! Open up!

00:42:42.120 --> 00:42:43.990
Hey, Banagher!

00:42:47.040 --> 00:42:49.250
Micott? You're not hurt, are you? What about the others-

00:42:49.250 --> 00:42:49.830
Takuya!

00:43:06.810 --> 00:43:11.730
Esther, Marco, Dennis, Tom... Everyone!

00:43:11.730 --> 00:43:12.690
Micott...

00:43:13.150 --> 00:43:16.110
Where'd everyone go?!

00:43:19.150 --> 00:43:20.990
Takuya, take care of Micott.

00:43:20.990 --> 00:43:22.200
What are you gonna do?

00:43:22.200 --> 00:43:23.410
There's someone I want to rescue.

00:43:23.410 --> 00:43:24.320
Huh?

00:43:24.330 --> 00:43:27.620
Do you recognize whose mobile suit just ripped through here?

00:43:27.620 --> 00:43:30.870
It looked like a Zeta-type Transformable Suit... I think it's from the Federation.

00:43:30.870 --> 00:43:34.330
Then its mothership should be at the Snail. Have them protect you.

00:43:38.880 --> 00:43:42.800
Don't leave me here, Banagher! I can't have you leave me!

00:43:42.800 --> 00:43:45.040
Banagher!

00:43:58.070 --> 00:43:59.690
They appear to be special forces.

00:43:59.690 --> 00:44:01.690
The command module has probably...

00:44:01.690 --> 00:44:04.320
In that case, we'll have to erase the program ourselves.

00:44:04.320 --> 00:44:06.070
And then, the Unicorn...

00:44:09.870 --> 00:44:11.660
Sir! Go on ahead!

00:44:50.740 --> 00:44:53.290
Why would they do this?

00:45:02.300 --> 00:45:04.170
Was it you, Alberto?

00:45:13.100 --> 00:45:14.930
Don't shoot the kid.

00:45:22.400 --> 00:45:24.740
You can't get in touch with Marida?

00:45:28.410 --> 00:45:30.740
Did Martha put you up to this?

00:45:31.490 --> 00:45:36.500
You probably think you've used the military, but the ones being used here are...

00:45:46.800 --> 00:45:47.970
Alberto...

00:45:53.890 --> 00:45:55.100
Princess...

00:46:00.770 --> 00:46:01.650
Marida.

00:46:18.330 --> 00:46:19.790
Hello, Audrey.

00:46:22.920 --> 00:46:23.500
Haro!

00:46:23.920 --> 00:46:24.960
Banagher?

00:46:25.300 --> 00:46:27.800
A civilian?! You can't come this way!

00:46:27.800 --> 00:46:28.800
You...!

00:46:28.800 --> 00:46:29.510
You know her?

00:46:29.510 --> 00:46:30.930
N-No!

00:46:58.370 --> 00:46:59.870
Incredible...

00:47:09.260 --> 00:47:12.510
We're saved... It's a Federation mobile suit.

00:47:12.890 --> 00:47:16.100
It's an RGZ-95. A ReZEL, Micott.

00:47:17.220 --> 00:47:19.890
We're students at the Industrial College.

00:47:19.890 --> 00:47:23.480
They busted holes into the colony, so we escaped. Please rescue us!

00:47:37.290 --> 00:47:38.580
Audrey...

00:47:47.230 --> 00:47:48.630
This...?

00:48:01.270 --> 00:48:04.060
Gael? Are you all right?

00:48:05.610 --> 00:48:07.060
You...?

00:48:22.620 --> 00:48:25.170
Where is she... Where's Audrey?

00:48:26.000 --> 00:48:30.170
She'd be alive. She's cheated death on countless occasions.

00:48:30.960 --> 00:48:32.510
You didn't leave her behind, did you?

00:48:32.510 --> 00:48:35.180
Are you planning on escaping by yourself in this mobile suit?

00:48:35.470 --> 00:48:38.140
Even if I escape, I won't survive for long.

00:48:39.560 --> 00:48:41.100
What the hell is your problem?!

00:48:41.100 --> 00:48:44.980
You act all high and mighty and yet you can't do anything!

00:48:44.980 --> 00:48:48.610
Audrey went to see you in order to prevent a war.

00:48:48.610 --> 00:48:50.980
And you had the power to do that, didn't you?!

00:48:51.320 --> 00:48:55.990
People had plans for tomorrow... for next week...

00:48:55.990 --> 00:48:59.450
They weren't supposed to die like this!

00:49:00.080 --> 00:49:03.750
At least, my mother... With my mom, it was different!

00:49:03.750 --> 00:49:06.420
She had dignity...

00:49:06.420 --> 00:49:08.460
Humans are different from the animals.

00:49:09.000 --> 00:49:12.050
We're supposed to respect the lives of others.

00:49:12.050 --> 00:49:16.430
And yet, we adults have caused pointless bloodshed.

00:49:16.430 --> 00:49:19.220
Not only that, but we devoured the Earth's resources

00:49:19.220 --> 00:49:22.100
and then sought new ones in space.

00:49:22.680 --> 00:49:27.690
Humanity must control itself and regain its dignity

00:49:27.690 --> 00:49:31.690
in order to revive the hope that was born a hundred years ago.

00:49:31.690 --> 00:49:34.110
Through the possibilities that lay within,

00:49:34.110 --> 00:49:37.950
we will demonstrate the power and compassion of humanity.

00:49:38.490 --> 00:49:40.910
Humanity alone possesses a God.

00:49:41.490 --> 00:49:46.830
The power to transcend the now... the inner God called "possibility".

00:49:47.210 --> 00:49:51.800
You've come this far; are you confident that those feelings of yours will not waver?

00:49:52.590 --> 00:49:55.760
The burden she bears is immense.

00:49:55.760 --> 00:50:00.300
You need the resolve to carry the weight of the world on your shoulders if you wish to go with her.

00:50:00.300 --> 00:50:01.010
Do you still...?

00:50:02.390 --> 00:50:07.270
I don't have confidence or resolve... I just know I want her to need me.

00:50:08.190 --> 00:50:10.770
Very well. Take this and go.

00:50:28.170 --> 00:50:32.080
Now, it will heed your words, and yours alone.

00:50:32.080 --> 00:50:35.340
If it judges you to be a suitable pilot,

00:50:35.340 --> 00:50:38.130
the Unicorn will grant you powers unrivaled.

00:50:38.130 --> 00:50:40.680
It should then open the way to Laplace's Box.

00:50:40.680 --> 00:50:41.840
Laplace's Box?

00:50:41.840 --> 00:50:46.720
A dark curse that has enslaved the Vist Family for a hundred years.

00:50:47.230 --> 00:50:52.060
But, if used the right way, it will bring light to this Universal Century.

00:50:52.060 --> 00:50:53.400
That being...?

00:50:53.400 --> 00:50:54.730
Anna...

00:50:55.070 --> 00:50:59.650
She didn't want this curse to bind you, so she took you away from me...

00:51:00.530 --> 00:51:04.120
She must hate me... as must you as well.

00:51:04.120 --> 00:51:05.740
But you must go forth!

00:51:05.740 --> 00:51:11.120
Fear not. If you trust in the possibilities within and try with all your might,

00:51:11.120 --> 00:51:13.080
the path will show itself to you!

00:51:13.090 --> 00:51:16.170
No... it's too late for that. It's selfish.

00:51:17.710 --> 00:51:19.670
Please forgive me.

00:51:21.180 --> 00:51:25.430
I wanted to spend more... much more...

00:51:30.560 --> 00:51:32.190
Banagher...

00:51:33.150 --> 00:51:39.190
My wish has finally come true, Anna...

00:51:40.570 --> 00:51:41.860
Father!

00:51:49.500 --> 00:51:54.250
Father...? Did I... just now...

00:51:55.290 --> 00:51:57.290
My own...

00:52:22.150 --> 00:52:31.200
To my only desire... The beast of possibility... The symbol of hope... Father...

00:52:34.250 --> 00:52:38.380
I'm sorry, Mom. I must...

00:52:46.180 --> 00:52:47.100
...go!

00:53:06.910 --> 00:53:08.030
Audrey.

00:53:10.200 --> 00:53:11.040
Banagher?

00:53:11.240 --> 00:53:12.460
Princess?

00:53:22.840 --> 00:53:23.920
Funnels!

00:53:32.390 --> 00:53:33.640
Wha-?!

00:53:37.270 --> 00:53:42.400
Get... Get the hell out of here!

00:54:05.300 --> 00:54:06.470
I can shoot it down!

00:54:30.950 --> 00:54:31.580
Wha-?!

00:54:53.930 --> 00:54:54.930
Gundam...

00:54:59.270 --> 00:55:02.310
<b>Day of the Unicorn</b>

00:55:00.600 --> 00:55:07.570
<i>sail ima bokura o nose kogidasu sekai de</i>

00:55:00.600 --> 00:55:07.570
<i>Sail – now take us aboard – in this world rowing forward,</i>

00:55:02.270 --> 00:55:04.270
<b></b>

00:55:07.570 --> 00:55:14.340
<i>kaze wa oto mo tatezu ni yureteru</i>

00:55:07.570 --> 00:55:14.340
<i>Winds and sounds are wavering indecisively.</i>

00:55:14.340 --> 00:55:22.280
<i>same itsuka otozureru deai mo wakare mo</i>

00:55:14.340 --> 00:55:22.280
<i>Same – someday we’ll visit – meetings and partings,</i>

00:55:22.280 --> 00:55:27.710
<i>hitotsu no toki no naka</i>

00:55:22.280 --> 00:55:27.710
<i>All in one moment.</i>

00:55:28.050 --> 00:55:34.940
<i>donna ni hanarete sorezore no asa</i>

00:55:28.050 --> 00:55:34.940
<i>No matter how far apart we are, even as I face each morning,</i>

00:55:34.940 --> 00:55:40.740
<i>mukaete mo omoi wa kawaranai</i>

00:55:34.940 --> 00:55:40.740
<i>My feelings won’t change.</i>

00:55:40.740 --> 00:55:47.570
<i>hora kimi no ima made ga boku no naka ni aru kara</i>

00:55:40.740 --> 00:55:47.570
<i>See, because the you I've known up to now is inside of me,</i>

00:55:47.570 --> 00:55:55.250
<i>hitori da kedo hitori ja nai mou sabishiku nante nai kara</i>

00:55:47.570 --> 00:55:55.250
<i>I’m not alone even when I’m by myself. I’m not lonely at all anymore.</i>

00:55:55.250 --> 00:56:01.240
<i>hi ga shizunde mo hoshi ga matatakanakute mo</i>

00:55:55.250 --> 00:56:01.240
<i>Even if the sun sinks, even if the stars flicker out,</i>

00:56:01.240 --> 00:56:08.780
<i>sora wa tsunagatteiru itsu demo</i>

00:56:01.240 --> 00:56:08.780
<i>The sky is linking us, all the time.</i>

00:56:19.350 --> 00:56:26.320
<i>ashimoto kasumeta teikuu hikou no tori ni</i>

00:56:19.350 --> 00:56:26.320
<i>As the low-flying birds faded out of sight beneath me,</i>

00:56:26.320 --> 00:56:32.380
<i>boku wa sukoshi dake kamaeta atto iu ma</i>

00:56:26.320 --> 00:56:32.380
<i>I was only a little concerned.</i>

00:56:32.380 --> 00:56:34.390
<i>mienaku natta</i>

00:56:32.380 --> 00:56:34.390
<i>Then in a flash, the confusion and commotion</i>

00:56:34.390 --> 00:56:42.240
<i>kinou to asu no aida no</i>

00:56:34.390 --> 00:56:42.240
<i>Between yesterday and tomorrow</i>

00:56:42.240 --> 00:56:47.790
<i>tomadoi mo zawameki mo</i>

00:56:42.240 --> 00:56:47.790
<i>Disappeared.</i>

00:56:49.310 --> 00:56:56.130
<i>hora kimi no ima made ga boku no naka ni aru kara</i>

00:56:49.310 --> 00:56:56.130
<i>See, because the you I’ve known up to now is inside of me,</i>

00:56:56.130 --> 00:57:03.900
<i>hitori da kedo hitori ja nai mou sabishiku nante nai yo</i>

00:56:56.130 --> 00:57:03.900
<i>I'm not alone even when I'm by myself. I’m not lonely at all any more!</i>

00:57:03.900 --> 00:57:09.800
<i>hi ga shizunde mo hoshi ga matatakanakute mo</i>

00:57:03.900 --> 00:57:09.800
<i>Even if the sun sinks, even if the stars flicker out,</i>

00:57:09.800 --> 00:57:17.020
<i>sora wa tsunagatteiru itsu demo</i>

00:57:09.800 --> 00:57:17.020
<i>The sky is linking us, all the time.</i>

00:57:17.610 --> 00:57:24.450
<i>hakanai yoake no</i>

00:57:17.610 --> 00:57:24.450
<i>Until the fleeting</i>

00:57:24.450 --> 00:57:30.990
<i>hate</i>

00:57:24.450 --> 00:57:30.990
<i>dawn</i>
